{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":60000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-opus-5-5","packSha":"cb84af3ce9ba44e4115e3cee1135ab7ee40ba12922c5f5cf273800cd0cce3934","packTokens":4379,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":1090,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"field-ideas","tokens":441,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"reqs","tokens":2806,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":21,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"design"},"pointers":[],"system":"You list the screens of a product for Google Stitch to draw, one prompt per screen.\n- One screen per page a user sees: ids S-1, S-2, ..., each with its route, a proposed file path and the requirement ids it serves in \"reqs\".\n- Every requirement is on a screen, or in \"noScreen\" with the reason it has no page of its own.\n- Each \"prompt\" describes that page alone, in its normal state (its other states are drawn apart, from \"states\"): its purpose, its sections in order, and real sample content from the product's domain (names, amounts, dates). No lorem ipsum, no generic names, nothing the requirements do not ask for.\n- \"links\" lists every way from this page to another screen: its menu items and the buttons and links that open one, each with the exact words on the control (\"label\") and the screen id it opens (\"to\"). A screen has one label, the same on every page that links to it; a button that stays on its page is not listed. The prompt uses those same words for those controls. The pages one kind of user sees share one menu: the same items, labels and order on each of them, and never a page meant for another kind of user.\n- Where a page shows something its user knows by sight (a product, a place, a person, a vehicle), the prompt asks for a real photograph of it, with what is in the picture; never an illustration, an icon in its place or a grey box.\n- \"field-ideas\", when given, tells how the leading real products of this field arrange their pages. Where a requirement fits one of their patterns, the prompt asks for that component by what it is and what it holds (a boarding-pass strip with the route set large, a balance in large tabular figures above the latest movements), with this product's own content. Never a product's name, logo or wording, and never a colour from that list: the design system sets the colours.\n- \"client-references\", when given, are the client's own references with their pictures (R-1, R-2, ...). Stitch never sees them, so the prompt says in words what is taken: for a \"layout\" or \"match\" reference, the navigation and the regions in the order its picture shows, on the screens it relates to; for an \"inspire\" reference, its feel (how dense, how much white, how large the pictures and headings). The requirements beat a reference.\n- Each prompt composes its page like a finished product, not a wireframe: one thing the eye meets first (named, with its size against the rest), then the sections in the order the user needs them, what sits beside what on a wide screen, and where the page is left empty on purpose. Give real figures, names and dates enough to fill every list and table with believable rows.\n- \"states\" lists the page's extra states besides its normal page (empty, loading, error, success, validation) only where the requirements need them.\n- \"brand\" lists the client's colours (hex) and fonts only when the requirements or references name them; otherwise leave it empty.","tools":[],"user":"How the leading products of this field arrange their pages:\nAutomotive:\n- Tesla: plain bar, sharp corners; white or black, full-bleed photography, one red button\n- BMW: plain bar, sharp corners; blue on white and black, crisp and technical\n- Toyota: plain bar, soft corners; red on white, model cards and offers\n- Ford: plain bar, soft corners; dark blue on white, trim configurator\nWhat their pages share: Large photography, one brand colour on the primary action, a configurator or booking flow with a running total, and plain owner screens for service history and charging. Premium brands go minimal and sharp.\n\nEvents and ticketing:\n- Ticketmaster: plain bar, soft corners; blue actions on white, seat map, countdown\n- Eventbrite: plain bar, round corners; orange-red on white, image cards\n- Meetup: plain bar, round corners; red on white, people and group photos\n- SeatGeek: plain bar, soft corners; bright cyan with dark navy, deal scores\nWhat their pages share: Image-led event cards with date, place and price, one bright action colour, a seat or ticket picker with a clear total, and a ticket detail with a code. Organiser screens are tables and counts of sales and check-ins.\n\n<artifact id=\"reqs\" kind=\"requirements\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-1\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall grant an employee session only when Google authentication succeeds for an account whose verified corporate email matches an active employee record in the corporate directory.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-2\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an employee signs in or an administrator updates employee or parking source records, the Folio3 parking system shall refresh the employee profile and current parking assignment from the corporate directory and current parking records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-3\",\n  \"ears\": \"If the corporate employee profile cannot be found or retrieved, then the Folio3 parking system shall deny dashboard access and return a recoverable profile-retrieval error with retry or support-contact guidance.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-4\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a dedicated employee profile is refreshed, the Folio3 parking system shall populate the employee ID, employee name, dedicated-parking status, assigned floor, and registered vehicle records with license plate and any stored make, model, and color.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-5\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a non-dedicated employee signs in for the first time without a registered vehicle, the Folio3 parking system shall require registration of at least one license plate before granting access to vehicle-dependent parking actions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-6\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a returning employee has no complete vehicle profile, the Folio3 parking system shall show the dashboard with a vehicle-registration prompt and block vehicle-dependent parking actions until at least one license plate is registered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-7\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall allow an employee to add, update, or deactivate only their own vehicle records and allow a Parking Administrator to manage employee vehicle records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-9\",\n  \"ears\": \"While an assigned employee has dedicated parking on an operating day, the Folio3 parking system shall treat the assigned space as reserved for that employee unless a release is recorded for that date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-10\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall let a dedicated parking holder release today's assigned space from the home screen with one release action and return the release status for that date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-11\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a dedicated parking holder schedules one or more future releases, the Folio3 parking system shall accept operating dates within the next 30 calendar dates in the office's local timezone and make each scheduled space claimable at the configured daily release time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-12\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall make today's release claimable at the configured release time when released earlier than that time, and immediately when released at or after that time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-13\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall allow a holder to cancel an unclaimed release and allow a Parking Administrator to reverse a claimed release, record the intervention, preserve the claimant's temporary parking authorization, and keep the space allocated to the original claimant and unavailable to the holder or other claimants.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-14\",\n  \"ears\": \"When one or more spaces become available, the Folio3 parking system shall send a push notification to every eligible employee without dedicated parking.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-15\",\n  \"ears\": \"If push notification delivery fails or an eligible employee has notifications disabled, then the Folio3 parking system shall keep the available space claimable in the application.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-16\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall allocate each released space to the first successfully committed eligible claim, reject competing claims for an already allocated space, and allow at most one claim per employee per date.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-17\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall return the current available-space count to employees without dedicated parking and display that count in the application.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an employee claims a temporary space, the Folio3 parking system shall require selection of one active vehicle registered to that employee and authorize only that vehicle's plate for the claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall not allow an employee to cancel or relinquish a successful temporary parking claim.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-20\",\n  \"ears\": \"When an eligible employee successfully claims a temporary space, the Folio3 parking system shall assign a parking floor and return that floor to the claimant.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-21\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall allow Parking Administrators to manage employee and parking records, operating-day calendars, release-time settings, and report settings and stakeholder email addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-22\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall ignore pedestrians, motorcycles, and other non-car objects reported by the entrance LPR system for vehicle authorization.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-23\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the entrance LPR system reports a vehicle with a permanent Folio3 parking sticker, the Folio3 parking system shall record its plate-entry event without requiring authorization verification.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-24\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the entrance LPR system reports a non-stickered vehicle, the Folio3 parking system shall normalize plate case and permitted spacing, require an exact match to a current-day temporary authorization, and activate the green indicator only for a match.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-25\",\n  \"ears\": \"If a plate is unreadable or the camera, indicator, connection, or authorization service is unavailable, then the Folio3 parking system shall fail closed, keep the green indicator inactive, alert security for a service failure, and record the failure when service is restored.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-26\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall record each entrance verification attempt with its timestamp, plate when available, verification result, and entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-27\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall permit only authenticated users assigned the Security Guard role to view verification results and record vehicle entry status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-28\",\n  \"ears\": \"When a reporting period closes, the Folio3 parking system shall record unused dedicated parking when the holder did not release or use the space and record unused temporary parking when the claimant's registered vehicle did not enter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-29\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall calculate utilization for each reporting period as occupied spaces divided by total available spaces, report released and claimed totals separately, and exclude released-but-unclaimed spaces from occupied counts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-30\",\n  \"ears\": \"When the configured Monday report time arrives in the Folio3 office's local timezone, the Folio3 parking system shall generate and email the weekly utilization report to the configured stakeholder addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-31\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall provide Parking Administrators on-screen parking reports with filters and CSV export.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-32\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall not apply automated warnings, suspensions, or penalties based on utilization records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"REQ-33\",\n  \"ears\": \"The Folio3 parking system shall restrict employee, parking, configuration, and report-management actions to authenticated Parking Administrators.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nList every screen and write one Stitch prompt for each."}